 PROXY protocol on both sides.
 Not doing so could introduce a security risk in your system (enabling request forgery).
 
+### PROXY Protocol Metadata
+
+A PROXY protocol version 2 header can carry arbitrary metadata as Type-Length-Value
+records (TLV). Traefik reads the TLV of type `0xF3`, and passes its value to the
+requests of that connection as the `X-Proxy-Meta` header.
+
+There is nothing to configure beyond `proxyProtocol` itself:
+
+```yaml tab="File (YAML)"
+## Static configuration
+entryPoints:
+  web:
+    address: ":80"
+    proxyProtocol:
+      trustedIPs:
+        - "10.0.0.0/8"
+```
+
+```toml tab="File (TOML)"
+## Static configuration
+[entryPoints]
+  [entryPoints.web]
+    address = ":80"
+
+    [entryPoints.web.proxyProtocol]
+      trustedIPs = ["10.0.0.0/8"]
+```
+
+```bash tab="CLI"
+## Static configuration
+--entryPoints.web.address=:80
+--entryPoints.web.proxyProtocol.trustedIPs=10.0.0.0/8
+```
+
+The header is set before the HTTP router matches, so routing rules and middlewares
+can both rely on it:
+
+```yaml tab="File (YAML)"
+## Routing configuration
+http:
+  routers:
+    tenant-acme:
+      entryPoints:
+        - web
+      rule: "Host(`example.com`) && Header(`X-Proxy-Meta`, `tenant=acme`)"
+      service: acme-backend
+```
+
+```toml tab="File (TOML)"
+## Routing configuration
+[http.routers]
+  [http.routers.tenant-acme]
+    entryPoints = ["web"]
+    rule = "Host(`example.com`) && Header(`X-Proxy-Meta`, `tenant=acme`)"
+    service = "acme-backend"
+```
+
+The value is passed as is: it is not decoded, unescaped, or trimmed. A TLV is
+ignored when its value is empty, or when it holds a byte outside of the printable
+ASCII range (`0x20`-`0x7E`), which rules out any header injection. When the PROXY
+protocol header carries several `0xF3` TLVs, `X-Proxy-Meta` holds one value per
+TLV, in the order they appear in the header, and the invalid ones are skipped.
+
+!!! info "The header cannot be forged"
+
+    An `X-Proxy-Meta` header sent by a client is always removed, on every
+    entryPoint, whether it enables `proxyProtocol` or not. A backend receiving
+    this header knows it comes from a TLV.
+
+    The metadata is only as trustworthy as the PROXY protocol header carrying it,
+    which the entryPoint `proxyProtocol.trustedIPs` and `proxyProtocol.insecure`
+    options already govern: the TLVs of a connection coming from an untrusted
+    address are ignored, exactly as its addresses are.
+
+!!! warning "HTTP/3"
+
+    HTTP/3 runs over QUIC, which has no PROXY protocol, so `X-Proxy-Meta` is never
+    set for an HTTP/3 request. It is still removed from the incoming request.
+
